<title>DUBAI: Bahrain applauds Clinton's re-election.</title>
<headline>Bahrain applauds Clinton's re-election.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bahrain on Wednesday congratulated U.S. President Bill Clinton on his re-election and said it was looking forward to stronger relations with the United States.</p>
<p>The official Gulf News Agency said the Emir Sheikh Isa bin Sulman al-Khalifa sent a message to Clinton &quot;conveying his best wishes on his re-election...and looking forward to stronger relations with the United States on all levels.&quot;</p>
<p>Bahrain is the administrative headquarters of the U.S. Navy's Fifth Fleet. In September it agreed to host U.S. military planes on the Gulf Arab island as part of a defence cooperation pact between the two countries.</p>
</text>
